  "lineage": "The shared popular-music field of Morocco, Algeria and Tunisia as it consolidated through state radio, cassette kiosks and the Paris migrant market from the 1950s onward — Andalusi modal inheritance and Arabic-Amazigh bilingual verse set to mandole, oud, violin, qanun and bendir, later synthesizer and drum machine, over 6/8 and shuffled 4/4 cycles with dense ornamentation, mawwal-style free vocal preludes, and choral refrains shared by chaabi, rai, malhun and Amazigh song.",
